[[File:Ancient Wyvern icon.png|left]]
'''Ancient Wyverns''' are [[Slayer monsters]] that require a [[Slayer]] level of 82 in order to be harmed. They reside in the [[Wyvern Cave]] on [[Fossil Island]] and are the strongest species of Wyvern in ''Old School RuneScape''. Like with other [[Wyverns]], an [[elemental shield]], [[mind shield]], [[dragonfire shield]], [[dragonfire ward]] or [[ancient wyvern shield]] provides significant protection against their [[icy breath]], and they are vulnerable to the effects of [[dragonbane weapons]]. These monsters require completion of the [[Bone Voyage]] quest to be assigned as a Slayer task.

In addition to being harder to fight, Ancient Wyverns share the ability with [[Taloned Wyvern]]s and [[Long-tailed Wyvern]]s to use a [[Typeless|typeless ranged]] attack that resembles a lighter coloured [[Water Blast]]. This attack ignores [[Protection prayers]] and hits for up to 10 damage, though it can also miss. They also use a [[Slash]] melee attack. When fighting them, the highest defensive [[armour]] the player can access is best suited to use against them. Should one choose to use ranged to fight them, it is recommended to fight in melee range and use Protect from Melee after de-aggroing the Wyverns.

Aggression can be removed by setting up a [[tolerance]] zone and staying within it.

